events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZazaGdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":349,"digest":"sha256:f6a3bc9e1b616d8e509e386652a3bd282cafb5c2b94f1be4880d541ca47f4392","download_count":18,"created_at":"2026-11-22T20:58:49Z","updated_at":"2026-11-22T20:58:49Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/ZazaGdev/FocusShell/releases/download/v2.1.0/latest.yml"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ZazaGdev/FocusShell/tarball/v2.1.0","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ZazaGdev/FocusShell/zipball/v2.1.0","body":"## FocusShell 2.1.0\n\nEverything added and fixed since 2.0.0 (10 November 2026).\n\n### Download\n\n- **Windows 10 and 11:** `FocusShell-Setup-2.1.0.exe`. If you have 2.0.0, the app finds this update by itself and asks before restarting. The installer is not code-signed: if SmartScreen stops it, click **More info**, then **Run anyway**.\n- **Mac (Apple silicon, macOS 14 or newer):** `FocusShell-2.1.0-arm64.dmg`. Open it and drag FocusShell to Applications. It is not signed by Apple, so macOS stops it the first time: open **System Settings > Privacy & Security**, scroll down and click **Open Anyway**. The Mac version cannot update itself: it tells you when a new version is out and opens this page.\n\nSHA-256, to check a download:\n\n- `FocusShell-Setup-2.1.0.exe`: 84ff4dda467fe0c2415f913883586f9048e3224f813156932764ccea5e172059\n- `FocusShell-2.1.0-arm64.dmg`: 20761912beca40f2216d9c960448c546988886bc13e1601a61f8486f5bb2ecee\n\n### New\n\n- **Leads plan, a builder writes the code.** For anything bigger than a small fix, a lead writes a plan and hands the coding to a builder agent on a model and effort that fit the task, then checks the work, has it reviewed and reports. A Waiting on you card shows which builder a lead used.\n- **Lighter builds for small projects:** mark a project `\"build\": \"light\"` in `projects.json` and its lead skips the stage-by-stage reviews: a cheaper builder and one short review at the end.\n- **Fewer tokens on long builds:** a new builder starts for each stage of a plan instead of carrying the whole plan's conversation, and each stage gets one combined review.\n- **Full panes start fresh:** when a lead's or the CTO's conversation gets very long, FocusShell asks it to stop at a safe point and reopens it fresh, and its unfinished tasks are sent again. The CTO also starts fresh each morning.\n- **Passing test runs and builds reach a lead as a short summary;** a failure still comes through in full.\n- **Copy on select:** selecting text in a pane copies it when you let go of the mouse, and programs in a pane can copy to the clipboard.\n- **Show done** on the boards lists every closed item, newest first, with the day it closed.\n- **The screen recorder is its own button**, on by default, with a short intro and a menu on its arrow. Plugins are on by default and each gets its own card in Settings.\n- **Waiting on you** lays its projects out in balanced columns with bolder project names.\n- Items can carry a start date, so the CTO picks them up on the right day.\n- Each lead in a project's split has its own border.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Clicking a link in a pane opens it in your browser after the warning (it showed the warning and then nothing).\n- Clicking a path to an `.html` file opens it in your browser instead of the code editor.\n- Typed words and card answers wait until a lead's input box is clear, and the card says when they did not arrive.\n- The check that typed words reached a lead also works when the project folder is reached through a junction or a second drive letter.\n- The app stays quicker in long sessions: panes, boards, links and the token counts read only what changed.\n- Tooltips wait two seconds every time, and the ones that said nothing useful are gone.\n- Maybe missed is removed.\n"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ZazaGdev/FocusShell/releases/43975827