:"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":349,"digest":"sha256:244bf0e993e48804501f0cb48e95d899ef68e8c582650c62a08f05280dd8d75d","download_count":35,"created_at":"2026-11-09T23:18:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-09T23:18:01Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/ZazaGdev/FocusShell/releases/download/v2.0.0/latest.yml"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ZazaGdev/FocusShell/tarball/v2.0.0","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ZazaGdev/FocusShell/zipball/v2.0.0","body":"## FocusShell 2.0.0\n\nEverything added and fixed since 1.0.0 (18 October 2026), and the first version for Apple silicon Macs.\n\n### Download\n\n- **Windows 10 and 11:** `FocusShell-Setup-2.0.0.exe`. If you already have 1.0.0, the app finds this update by itself and asks before restarting. The installer is not code-signed: if SmartScreen stops it, click **More info**, then **Run anyway**.\n- **Mac (Apple silicon, macOS 14 or newer):** `FocusShell-2.0.0-arm64.dmg`. Open it and drag FocusShell to Applications. It is not signed by Apple, so macOS stops it the first time: open **System Settings > Privacy & Security**, scroll down and click **Open Anyway**. The Mac version cannot update itself: it tells you when a new version is out and opens this page.\n\nSHA-256, to check a download:\n\n- `FocusShell-Setup-2.0.0.exe`: 6f55e647e309358bf8fe8b49269a520221834b24dbd37eb6a46014efb4bc02db\n- `FocusShell-2.0.0-arm64.dmg`: 6e65ab500fc626ea726dbd8909ee74731dcd0ba4c109f2bf6c33ed61c51ed2c8\n\n### New\n\n- **FocusShell on a Mac:** the Mac menu and Cmd shortcuts, the Code pane with your VS Code, talk to the CTO from any app and hold Ctrl to draw, the microphone button on a card starts Dictation, and the screen recorder with `ffmpeg` and `whisper-cpp` from Homebrew. macOS asks once for each permission these use.\n- **Leads pick an effort level for each task**, from a label change to a security fix, and say which one they picked.\n- **Up to five leads per project**, and Ctrl+click a lead's number to see a project's leads side by side in its pane.\n- **Waiting on you cards are easier to read:** a short plain summary of each question, the time each item started waiting, an X to dismiss a card (with Undo), and images pasted or dropped into a card's Answer box. A card you answered leaves the list.\n- **Screen recorder:** pick an area on any monitor, a list of your recorded videos with Regenerate tasks and Talk to agent, a mic icon on the floating bar that lights while it hears you, and hold Ctrl to draw while recording (Ctrl+Alt+Backspace clears).\n- **The CTO opens a file you ask for** in its project's Code pane, beside that project's lead, and opens and closes panes through commands that work on Windows and a Mac.\n- **Settings > Projects** shows each project on its own row with its folder, a Claude model picker per project, and a remove that asks first.\n- **Classic view switch:** start sessions in Claude Code's classic view, so a pane keeps its whole history and Find searches all of it.\n- **One tooltip style everywhere,** also shown on keyboard focus; the project tab tooltip waits a second so a quick pass over the tabs stays quiet.\n- Panes the CTO opens start in the background, and Today on Self gets a sort picker.\n- The uninstaller offers an unticked \"Also delete my FocusShell data\" box. Updates and silent uninstalls never delete your data.\n- The app keeps its large caches in AppData\\Local, and asks before the Code pane first downloads VS Code's server.\n- A guide to how FocusShell works with Claude Code's permissions: [PERMISSIONS.md](https://github.com/ZazaGdev/FocusShell/blob/main/PERMISSIONS.md).\n\n### Fixed\n\n- A lead's tab dot lights only while that lead is working, and stays lit while its background shells or subagents still run.\n- A project whose folder name holds characters such as brackets, &, % or ! now starts.\n- The Start menu shortcut opens the app.\n- Links in panes and cards: paths with spaces, paths wrapped mid-word, URLs next to punctuation and list lines after a link are all handled correctly, and no stray link colour is left behind.\n- A lead's tab dot is orange only while that lead is waiting on you.\n- Waiting on you keeps the card you are reading, and your Answer text, in place when other cards come and go.\n- A lead's question card shows the question and its options in full.\n- Lines typed into a pane wait while you dictate or write a prompt there; Status refresh waits until you are idle.\n- Closing a board card keeps its column's scroll position; Done and Send stay inside a crowded card.\n- Recorder cards go to the project on screen and reach the CTO.\n- Maybe missed finds the CTO's log after Claude was restarted by hand in its pane.\n"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ZazaGdev/FocusShell/releases/416757637","assets_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ZazaGdev/FocusShell/releases/416757637/assets","upload_url":"https://uploads.github.com/repos/ZazaGdev/FocusShell/releases/416757637/assets{?name,label}","html_url":"https://github.com/ZazaGdev/FocusShell/releases/tag/v1.0.0","id":416757637,"author":{"login":"ZazaGdev","id":75507663,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1NTA3NjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75507663?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZazaGdev","html_url":"https://github.com/ZazaGdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZazaGdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZazaGdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZazaGdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZazaGdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZazaGdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZazaGdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZazaGdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZazaGdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https: